# Smol Biscuits SlimeVR Trackers
These are a derivative of SlimeVR trackers, designed to be smaller, lighter and longer lasting!

They consists of:
- Custom PCB
- Custom 3D printed case
- Custom firmware derived from SlimeVR firmware

## PCB
The PCB is designed in KiCad and the files can be found in the `pcb` folder. The PCB is designed to be as small as possible, acting as a carrier board for a Seeed Studio XIAO nrf52840 on the opposite side of the sensors.

The sensor board has an IMU and a magnetometer.

### IMU
> ICM-45686

### Magnetometer
> QMC-6309

## Battery
The board requires a LiPo batter. Size based on your needs, but the included case is designed to fit a 150mAh battery.

## 3D Printed Case
The case is a two-piece design with a flexible interlink. The battery is in one case and the PCB in the other.

The flexi-link allows the two piece design to bend around the body and also forms part of the strain relief for the battery cable.

The case files can be found in the `case` folder.

### Materials
- The flexi-link is designed to be printed in TPU.
- The base plates should be printed in PETG for strength. The strap piece is put under strain and may break if printed in PLA.
- The top cover can be printed in PLA or PETG, whatever you prefer.
- The switch can also be printed in whatever you prefer for aesthetics.

## Firmware
### Pre-Compiled Firmware
The firmware is added as a git submodule in the `firmware` folder. It is a fork of the SlimeVR firmware with support for the Smol Biscuits PCB.

To program the trackers and receiver you can use the pre-compiled firmware files included in the releases section of this repository.

### Compiling the Firmware Yourself
In order to compile the firmware yourself, you will need to follow the instructions in the SlimeVR firmware repository, with the following changes:
1. Clone this repository with `--recurse-submodules` to get the firmware submodule.
2. Open the firmware folder and follow the instructions on the SlimeVR dev page: https://docs.slimevr.dev/smol-slimes/firmware/smol-compiling-firmware.html
3. When compiling the tracker, use the command: `west build -p auto -b xiao_ble -d build . -- -DNCS_TOOLCHAIN_VERSION=NONE -DBOARD_ROOT=.` to select the correct board.

## Assembly
### Soldering the PCB
1. Solder the sensor components onto the PCB. Leave the XIAO nrf52840 off for now.
2. Pre-tin the battery terminals on the XIAO and it's footprint on the PCB.
3. Using the solder jig, place the XIAO nrf52840 with the battery terminals facing up.
4. Apply flux.
5. Place the sensor PCB on top of the XIAO, aligning the battery terminals.
6. Use the square heat pass-through pads to melt the solder, applying slight pressure to flatten the board to the XIAO.
7. Allow to cool and inspect the joints. Use a multimeter to check for shorts.
8. Solder all of the castellated pins around the edge of the PCB.
9. Solder the battery to the back of the sensor board.

### Programming the PCB
1. Connect the XIAO nrf52840 to your computer using a USB-C cable
2. Put the XIAO into bootloader mode by double-tapping the reset button
3. Copy the bootloader firmware (
`update-slimenrf_xiao_sense_bootloader-0.9.2-SlimeVR.7_nosd.uf2` ) file to the XIAO drive.
4. The XIAO will reboot and show up as a new drive called `SLIMENRF_XIAO_SENSE`. If it does not, repeat step 2.
5. Copy the tracker firmware ( `firmware_tracker.uf2` ) file to the `SLIMENRF_XIAO_SENSE` drive.
6. The XIAO will reboot and start running the firmware.

### Programming the Receiver
Depending on the receiver you are using, you may need to refer to the SlimeVR documentation for programming instructions.

For the Holyiot receiver, you can use the pre-compiled firmware file ( `firmware_receiver.hex` ) and use nordic nrf connect programmer to flash the firmware to the Holyiot board.

### Set-up and calibration
Refer to the SlimeVR documentation for setting up and calibrating the trackers in the SlimeVR software.
https://docs.slimevr.dev/smol-slimes/firmware/smol-pairing-and-calibration.html

### Assembling the Case
1. Slide the bases onto a 30mm strap. Make sure the notches are facing eachother.
2. Place the flex link between the bases in its slot.
3. Insert the battery spacer between the strap and battery, then place the battery on top.
4. Holding the battery in place by it's wires, place the battery base on top and snap it into place.
5. Place the PCB into the PCB base, ensuring the switch is aligned with the cutout.
6. Slide the switch slider over the PCB switch.
7. Ensuring the case correctly slides over the switch, snap the top cover into place.
8. Adjust the strap to fit and secure it in place.

---

And that's it! Your Smol Biscuits SlimeVR trackers are ready to use! 🎊